  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - On 18/08/2025, the existing use of a room within the dwellinghouse for the taking of bookings by telephone and email in relation to the private hire business is ancillary to the property's use as a single family dwellinghouse and is lawful within the meaning of Section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reason:\r\n\r\nThe private hire booking business within the property amounts to the receipt of bookings by telephone, and there is only one operator at the premises. No external alterations are proposed.  There is no picking up or dropping off of customers at the site or comings and goings of drivers to the premises.  The nature and scale of the business use would not amount to a material change of use of part or whole of the house and therefore planning permission is not required.\r\n"
